description:
Aquazzura is a luxury footwear brand founded in Florence in 2011 by Colombian designer **Edgardo Osorio**.


Rooted in Italian craftsmanship and driven by a contemporary, feminine vision, Aquazzura is known for its refined elegance, exceptional comfort and timeless yet modern design. Each collection reflects a perfect balance between tradition and innovation, with a strong focus on quality, detail and savoir\-faire.


Today, Aquazzura is an internationally recognized brand, distributed in over 50 countries, with headquarters in Florence and Milan and boutiques in the world’s most prestigious luxury destinations.






**Posizione:**
--------------

The Stock \& Runner Associate is responsible for receiving, storing, and managing the inventory of merchandise and supplies in a timely and organized manner, contributing to the profitability of the boutique’s operations and also supporting the Sales team with stock\-related activities, including product retrieval, replenishment, transfers, and maintaining an organized stockroom.

**Main duties:**

* Assist with all inbound and outbound merchandise based on weekly shipments, intra boutique transfers, EOS returns, consignments, client returns and other merchandise movements as per your Store Manager directives;
* Manage and organize the stock in accordance with AQUAZZURA procedures and directives;
* Guarantee receipt, quantities, deliveries of articles and supplies;
* Ensure replenishment of products from other locations based on latest sales trend and OH analysis on a weekly basis;
* Prepare new items to be displayed on shop floor in collaboration with the sales team and in accordance with the VM set up guidelines received;
* Control and organize transfers and other stock operations;
* Manage daily / weekly placement of articles for sale;
* Support monthly cycle counts and official inventories as per directives sent from HQ
* Support planning and handling of inventory activities.
* Communicate and resolve any issues with the Retail System in a timely manner

**Requisiti:**
--------------

* The ideal candidate must have 2/3 years’ experience in a similar role in fashion and luxury contexts;
* Excellent organizational skills;
* Accuracy, punctuality and flexibility will be considered essential features.
* Fluent in Spanish and English, other languages are a plus.
